1
00:00:05,463 --> 00:00:06,506
A documentary?

2
00:00:06,589 --> 00:00:09,134
Do you know a show called
<i>Document Memoreal?</i>

3
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:10,051
I know it.

4
00:00:10,135 --> 00:00:11,928
It's that famous
day-in-the-life show, right?

5
00:00:12,011 --> 00:00:16,266
That show called and said
they want to do a feature on me.

6
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:18,059
Say what?

7
00:00:18,143 --> 00:00:19,853
Maybe I'll turn it down.

8
00:00:19,936 --> 00:00:22,605
<i>Actors are supposed to keep</i>
<i>their private lives a mystery!</i>

9
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:25,191
You can't afford
to have such picky standards!

10
00:00:26,276 --> 00:00:27,527
I guess I'll take it!

11
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:31,990
<i>He definitely thinks he'll go viral</i>
<i>and become popular after the show.</i>

12
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:34,534
<i>I wonder if things</i>
<i>will really go that well.</i>

13
00:00:35,118 --> 00:00:37,746
Good morning.
I'm Torihara from <i>Document Memoreal</i>.

14
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:39,622
This is my manager.

15
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:40,540
Konta…

16
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:41,750
Just play along.

17
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:44,085
I look forward to working with you all!

18
00:00:44,169 --> 00:00:45,462
The pleasure is ours!

19
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:46,796
Thank you.

20
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:20,997
I practice every day,

21
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:24,334
so that I'm ready no matter
what kind of role comes my way.

22
00:01:24,417 --> 00:01:26,127
You are an example for all actors.

23
00:01:26,711 --> 00:01:29,339
After stage combat practice,
I go for a run.

24
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:33,885
This is my usual routine,
so Torihara, let's go.

25
00:01:34,385 --> 00:01:37,806
He's never gone for a run even once.

26
00:01:38,556 --> 00:01:40,183
-Midori!
-What?

27
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:43,061
Make today's BBQ extra fancy!
So it looks good on camera.

28
00:01:43,144 --> 00:01:44,020
What's that about?

29
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:47,565
Put it on skewers to make it look nice.
Buy some good meat too. Beef please!

30
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:50,360
Our usual meat should be fine!
I'm even making sauce for it.

31
00:01:50,443 --> 00:01:52,445
I don't want people to find out I'm poor!

32
00:01:52,529 --> 00:01:53,530
Pork also tastes good!

33
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:57,742
-Please! Beef please!
-Are you that desperate?

34
00:01:58,368 --> 00:02:00,036
The sea feels good, right?

35
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,871
-It's nice.
-Pleasant, right?

36
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:03,790
Wait a second…

37
00:02:04,999 --> 00:02:08,878
For us actors,
our bodies are our greatest asset.

38
00:02:08,962 --> 00:02:12,090
So… I spare nothing…
when it comes to training.

39
00:02:12,173 --> 00:02:13,424
You're amazing.

40
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:17,220
Um… Four tomatoes cost 200 yen,

41
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:19,139
but I only want to buy one.

42
00:02:19,222 --> 00:02:20,140
Not all four?

43
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:22,100
I only need one right now.

44
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:24,727
I'm not great at division.

45
00:02:24,811 --> 00:02:28,022
I'm better at multiplication.
But anyway, how much for one?

46
00:02:28,106 --> 00:02:28,898
It's 50 yen.

47
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:30,775
-Fifty?
-Yeah.

48
00:02:30,859 --> 00:02:31,860
You didn't know?

49
00:02:31,943 --> 00:02:33,111
-I did know.
-You did?

50
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:36,156
Twenty, forty, fifty… Okay.

51
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,994
Can you cut what we just said?

52
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:41,911
Sure.

53
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:43,955
-For us actors…
-Yes.

54
00:02:44,038 --> 00:02:45,456
-Our body is our capital.
-Yes.

55
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:47,584
So I'm careful about what I eat.

56
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:50,253
Oh, that's great.

57
00:02:50,336 --> 00:02:51,296
Okay.

58
00:02:51,379 --> 00:02:52,547
So good.

59
00:02:54,048 --> 00:02:55,216
Huh?

60
00:02:56,134 --> 00:02:58,303
I can really taste the sun.

61
00:02:58,887 --> 00:03:01,055
-Wow, tomatoes really suit you.
-Mr. Nishigami!

62
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:21,576
Mr. Konta. I was just about
to come over and deliver some fish.

63
00:03:21,659 --> 00:03:23,286
Yay, awesome!

64
00:03:23,369 --> 00:03:26,289
Mr. Nishigami, today's barbecue
is super fancy, so why don't you join us?

65
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:28,666
-May I?
-Of course.

66
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:31,461
-Mr. Konta. Who is this man?
-Huh?

67
00:03:31,544 --> 00:03:34,130
-Huh? Are you curious about him?
-Yes.

68
00:03:34,213 --> 00:03:35,381
Well…

69
00:03:36,174 --> 00:03:39,552
This is Mr. Nishigami.
He manages this entire area.

70
00:03:41,512 --> 00:03:42,722
Wow.

71
00:03:42,805 --> 00:03:44,307
What a handsome man.

72
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:47,894
Mr. Torihara.

73
00:03:47,977 --> 00:03:51,147
Please don't film that man.
He's just a regular person.

74
00:03:51,231 --> 00:03:54,859
He's regular people.
Please film me. I'm the professional here.

75
00:03:54,943 --> 00:03:57,528
He's just an ordinary guy,
totally ordinary.

76
00:03:57,612 --> 00:04:00,323
It's just that he's quite tall,
has a small face,

77
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:01,532
and he's cool too!

78
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:04,077
Who's that, Chainsaw Woman?

79
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,787
Please film me!

80
00:04:06,913 --> 00:04:08,915
-What was that noise?
-Sorry.

81
00:04:10,625 --> 00:04:12,961
Our food looks fancy today.

82
00:04:13,044 --> 00:04:15,129
I'm just putting them on skewers, though.

83
00:04:15,213 --> 00:04:17,131
But I actually bought beef.

84
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:19,842
We need to save money later.

85
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:24,222
It would be great
if this really makes Konta successful.

86
00:04:25,348 --> 00:04:26,933
I'm worried.

87
00:04:27,016 --> 00:04:29,227
It's like my brother
has completely changed

88
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,271
since the show started.

89
00:04:32,772 --> 00:04:33,898
No! The meat!

90
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:36,651
-Oh, crap…
-It's fine. I'll do it. Give.

91
00:04:40,905 --> 00:04:45,702
He doesn't need to put on a show.
I prefer him as he is.

92
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:50,331
You like him as he is?

93
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:07,974
Mr. Nishigami!

94
00:05:08,891 --> 00:05:10,268
I'm doing an interview now.

95
00:05:10,852 --> 00:05:13,187
-An interview.
-But this needs doing.

96
00:05:13,271 --> 00:05:16,399
But, I'm doing an interview.
Please quiet down a bit.

97
00:05:16,482 --> 00:05:17,984
Please! Just a little bit.

98
00:05:18,067 --> 00:05:19,652
One more time.

99
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:20,987
Once more?

100
00:05:22,238 --> 00:05:24,699
You look great. Like a magazine cover.

101
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:28,369
A magazine cover, huh?
I would love to do one.

102
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:31,164
"I'll buy it because Konta Hoshino
is on the cover."

103
00:05:31,247 --> 00:05:33,583
"I'll watch it
because Konta Hoshino is in it."

104
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:37,962
I want to create
a Konta Hoshino sensation like that.

105
00:05:38,588 --> 00:05:39,922
That's nice.

106
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:42,383
<i>Hey, Mr. Nishigami!</i>

107
00:05:42,467 --> 00:05:45,094
<i>Hey, are you filming me?</i>

108
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:47,013
-Are you?
-That was a group shot.

109
00:05:47,096 --> 00:05:48,473
Please do it right.

110
00:05:52,643 --> 00:05:53,644
Excuse me.

111
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:55,438
<i>It's a call from…</i>

112
00:05:56,272 --> 00:05:58,316
<i>the actor Jin Ichijo.</i>

113
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:00,985
<i>-May I take it?</i>
<i>-Go ahead.</i>

114
00:06:03,112 --> 00:06:05,615
<i>Hello, Mr. Jin? Yeah, what's up?</i>

115
00:06:06,282 --> 00:06:08,367
<i>Oh, the other day.</i>

116
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:10,661
<i>No, thank you! Yeah.</i>

117
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:15,666
<i>Come hang out any time.</i>
<i>All right, have a nice summer vacation!</i>

118
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:19,837
Wait, do you know Jin Ichijo?

119
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:21,422
We are acquaintances.

120
00:06:22,006 --> 00:06:23,382
-I've acted with him too.
-What?

121
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:25,343
-We're basically bros.
-Wow!

122
00:06:25,426 --> 00:06:29,764
We have a great
give-and-take relationship.

123
00:06:29,847 --> 00:06:32,225
That's amazing.

124
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:34,894
Excuse me…

125
00:06:34,977 --> 00:06:36,145
Yes?

126
00:06:36,229 --> 00:06:39,190
-Just a moment. Hold on.
-What's wrong?

127
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:42,068
Hello, Mr. Jin?

128
00:06:42,151 --> 00:06:44,946
No, that's not it. I'm sorry.

129
00:06:45,029 --> 00:06:48,241
I'm filming for a show
called <i>Document Memoreal</i>.

130
00:06:48,324 --> 00:06:52,286
Yes, exactly. So, I guess
I got too excited.

131
00:06:52,829 --> 00:06:54,455
Sorry. I'm sorry.

132
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:56,791
Thank you very much. I'll do my best.

133
00:06:56,874 --> 00:07:00,253
By the way, Mr. Jin,
give me some work once in a while.

134
00:07:00,336 --> 00:07:03,256
No matter how small the role…
Even a tiny role. I'll do it.

135
00:07:03,339 --> 00:07:06,884
Yes, please. Goodbye.

136
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:12,515
-Hey, stop the camera!
-Sorry.

137
00:07:12,598 --> 00:07:14,016
By the way, what was that?

138
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,184
What?

139
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:17,145
Just utilities.

140
00:07:17,228 --> 00:07:18,604
-Utilities?
-They called me…

141
00:07:18,688 --> 00:07:20,273
Konta, let's start the barbecue.

142
00:07:20,356 --> 00:07:21,566
Okay!

143
00:07:21,649 --> 00:07:23,734
Oh, I'll make a drink for you.

144
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:24,652
You will?

145
00:07:24,735 --> 00:07:27,488
-But cut out that part earlier.
-Okay.

146
00:07:27,572 --> 00:07:31,951
Konta Hoshino doesn't
squeeze it like this, but like this!

147
00:07:32,034 --> 00:07:34,203
-Oh, nice. How dynamic.
-Like this!

148
00:07:34,287 --> 00:07:36,289
Then with my other hand…

149
00:07:36,372 --> 00:07:38,708
-Like this!
-Oh, very nice.

150
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:41,002
Mr. Manager.

151
00:07:41,085 --> 00:07:42,170
Mr. Manager.

152
00:07:42,253 --> 00:07:44,338
Yes? Oh, me?

153
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:47,467
If you have any footage
of his past works or audition tapes,

154
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:49,510
could we borrow them to use as material?

155
00:07:50,344 --> 00:07:51,971
Materials, got it.

156
00:07:52,054 --> 00:07:53,014
Thanks.

157
00:07:53,097 --> 00:07:55,057
Mr. Torihara. I'll make you a drink.

158
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:57,101
But I'm still on the clock.

159
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:58,227
It's totally fine.

160
00:07:58,311 --> 00:08:01,314
However, if you drink this,
you'll turn stupid!

161
00:08:01,397 --> 00:08:02,190
What?

162
00:08:02,273 --> 00:08:06,444
Okay, it's time for
Konta Hoshino's half-assed cooking!

163
00:08:07,653 --> 00:08:11,282
So, you know the familiar
lemon sour mix and gum syrup.

164
00:08:11,365 --> 00:08:14,035
Normally, you put them in one by one,
but I'm an expert.

165
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:18,331
I'll just pour them in at the same time.
Pouring them in. I'll just eyeball it.

166
00:08:18,414 --> 00:08:19,790
I'm even closing my eyes.

167
00:08:19,874 --> 00:08:23,377
-Konta, stop!
-This much should be about right. More!

168
00:08:23,461 --> 00:08:26,964
I'll squint and check.
This should be enough, right?

169
00:08:27,048 --> 00:08:29,509
-Next, pour in the soda.
-Yes.

170
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:33,095
Fizz… I'm also eyeballing it
while closing my eyes.

171
00:08:33,179 --> 00:08:34,180
You close your eyes?

172
00:08:34,263 --> 00:08:35,932
Is this about right?

173
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:37,725
-Konta!
-Just in time!

174
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:42,146
Here you go, Mr. Torihara.
It's done. Drink up!

175
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:43,773
Oh, thank you.

176
00:08:43,856 --> 00:08:45,066
Go ahead.

177
00:08:49,278 --> 00:08:50,488
It has a stupid taste.

178
00:08:50,571 --> 00:08:52,657
Yeah, exactly. It makes you stupid.

179
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:58,871
Midori, you're awesome!

180
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:00,039
You bought beef.

181
00:09:00,122 --> 00:09:01,666
Yeah, I did.

182
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:06,295
This is <i>acqua pazza</i> made with
the sea bream Mr. Nishigami brought us!

183
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:07,838
What's <i>acqua pazza</i>?

184
00:09:07,922 --> 00:09:09,799
-It's <i>acqua pazza</i>.
-What is "<i>pazza</i>"?

185
00:09:09,882 --> 00:09:10,967
What?

186
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:13,261
What's with your reaction?

187
00:09:13,344 --> 00:09:15,680
Did you make this, Ms. Midori?

188
00:09:15,763 --> 00:09:19,058
Yes. It's full of nature's blessings.

189
00:09:21,602 --> 00:09:23,062
It's beautiful.

190
00:09:24,730 --> 00:09:26,065
Let's eat, okay?

191
00:09:26,148 --> 00:09:28,067
-Looks delicious, for sure.
-Go ahead.

192
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:30,444
-It looks great.
-Slide it out…

193
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:33,739
Done!

194
00:09:33,823 --> 00:09:35,032
Here, Mr. Nishigami.

195
00:09:35,116 --> 00:09:36,742
Thank you very much.

196
00:09:36,826 --> 00:09:41,038
My little sister is a genius at cooking.
Everything she makes tastes amazing!

197
00:09:41,122 --> 00:09:42,331
That's impressive.

198
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:44,625
Mr. Torihara, you don't need
to keep filming. Let's eat.

199
00:09:44,709 --> 00:09:46,252
-What?
-I'll serve some for you, here.

200
00:09:46,335 --> 00:09:47,420
All right.

201
00:09:47,503 --> 00:09:49,880
Wait, Konta, that's too much.

202
00:09:49,964 --> 00:09:52,883
Mr. Torihara has been filming me
all day today.

203
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:56,262
His stomach must be rumbling,
so he needs to eat at least this much.

204
00:09:56,345 --> 00:09:58,764
-Thank you very much.
-Come on, give me the camera.

205
00:09:58,848 --> 00:10:00,308
Maybe I'll film.

206
00:10:01,309 --> 00:10:04,770
-It's all just salad.
-A gathering of amateurs!

207
00:10:04,854 --> 00:10:07,773
A gathering of amateurs!
We're all amateurs, all right.

208
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:08,691
That's true.

209
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:13,362
Mr. Konta, have you ever
held a regular job?

210
00:10:13,446 --> 00:10:14,905
A job, huh…

211
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:18,451
Acting is my true calling.

212
00:10:19,535 --> 00:10:22,371
I will be an actor forever.

213
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:24,373
Then what about part-time jobs?

214
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:26,417
Right, yes.

215
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:29,712
I've done various part-time jobs.

216
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:34,800
But I believe all of it
feeds into my acting.

217
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,471
By the way, what about now?

218
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:41,891
Oh, I focus solely on acting.

219
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:47,146
I only do part-time jobs occasionally,
for role research.

220
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:53,027
Why did you decide to become an actor?

221
00:10:58,949 --> 00:11:04,789
When I was in the third grade,
I acted in <i>Momotaro </i>for a school play.

222
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:08,959
At that time, it was so much fun.

223
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:12,380
I just had a very minor role, though.

224
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:16,801
Being able to become someone
other than myself

225
00:11:17,468 --> 00:11:21,472
to me, was a very happy moment.

226
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:26,936
I think, I was born to act.

227
00:11:27,019 --> 00:11:30,106
I was born for that purpose.
I truly believe that.

228
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:34,026
Midori also supports me.

229
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:38,948
Everyone is supporting me,
so I want to get on top,

230
00:11:40,491 --> 00:11:41,951
for their sake.

231
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:55,589
Torihara, I saw the footage you got.

232
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:59,343
It's good. But if we inflate his ego more,
we can film something way funnier.

233
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:01,929
Yes, but about that…

234
00:12:02,012 --> 00:12:07,059
Let him run amok,
and give us lots of smug faces.

235
00:12:08,477 --> 00:12:12,606
It's better to exaggerate things.
That's what the viewers are looking for.

236
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:15,943
Yes.

237
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:17,820
I understand.

238
00:12:29,832 --> 00:12:31,000
Good morning.

239
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:32,251
Oh, good morning.

240
00:12:32,334 --> 00:12:33,794
Where is Mr. Konta?

241
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:35,588
He left a little while ago.

242
00:12:35,671 --> 00:12:38,007
Lately, he has been going out
a lot in the morning.

243
00:12:38,090 --> 00:12:39,717
But I think he'll be back soon.

244
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:41,385
It's so early. Where did he go?

245
00:12:42,011 --> 00:12:45,473
It seems he's helping out the neighbors.

246
00:12:45,556 --> 00:12:46,724
Helping out?

247
00:12:46,807 --> 00:12:49,560
Oh! But I don't think
he wants that part to be filmed.

248
00:12:49,643 --> 00:12:50,853
But I've got to film that!

249
00:12:50,936 --> 00:12:53,439
Huh? No, maybe you shouldn't?

250
00:12:53,522 --> 00:12:54,940
I'll just go check it out.

251
00:12:55,024 --> 00:12:57,318
-Huh? Wait…
-I'm off!

252
00:12:58,777 --> 00:12:59,778
Oh, boy.

253
00:13:02,406 --> 00:13:03,657
Well, not my problem.

254
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:07,745
Good morning, ma'am!

255
00:13:07,828 --> 00:13:09,705
All right, shall we get to it?

256
00:13:09,788 --> 00:13:11,290
Sorry for making you do this.

257
00:13:11,373 --> 00:13:13,584
Don't be. You look beautiful today too.

258
00:13:13,667 --> 00:13:14,585
Thank you.

259
00:13:14,668 --> 00:13:15,628
All right!

260
00:13:17,796 --> 00:13:19,131
-Konta.
-Yes!

261
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:21,342
I have some tea here.
Make sure to drink it.

262
00:13:21,425 --> 00:13:25,054
Oh, thank you. Hup.

263
00:13:25,137 --> 00:13:26,931
Hup!

264
00:13:27,014 --> 00:13:30,559
Wait! That isn't a weed. Don't pull it.

265
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:32,394
Huh? This isn't a weed?

266
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:34,313
It's mugwort I'm carefully growing.

267
00:13:34,396 --> 00:13:36,398
Oh, ma'am, I'm sorry.

268
00:13:36,482 --> 00:13:38,150
My goodness Konta…

269
00:13:38,234 --> 00:13:39,360
Wait, can you eat this?

270
00:13:39,443 --> 00:13:40,611
Yes, you can.

271
00:13:43,447 --> 00:13:46,742
Oh, you're right.
It tastes like mugwort mochi.

272
00:13:47,451 --> 00:13:48,452
Wow, it's good.

273
00:13:49,245 --> 00:13:50,079
I can't stop.

274
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:51,580
It's good.

275
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:53,290
It's actually good!

276
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:55,125
Come on, don't eat so much.

277
00:13:55,209 --> 00:13:56,126
Do you want some?

278
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:57,127
What?

279
00:13:57,211 --> 00:13:59,630
Please make some mugwort mochi with this.

280
00:13:59,713 --> 00:14:00,756
-What? With this?
-Yes.

281
00:14:00,839 --> 00:14:04,218
Mugwort mochi is just mugwort
and rice cake, so you can make it, right?

282
00:14:04,301 --> 00:14:05,219
It's not that simple.

283
00:14:05,302 --> 00:14:06,679
Oh, I see.

284
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:10,182
-Konta.
-Yes?

285
00:14:10,266 --> 00:14:12,142
Thanks for your hard work. Have this.

286
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:14,270
Huh?

287
00:14:15,688 --> 00:14:17,356
Thank you!

288
00:14:18,315 --> 00:14:21,277
Mrs. Kawamoto next door
wants to ask you to walk Pero.

289
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:24,655
-Okay. See you later.
-Get on it, okay?

290
00:14:24,738 --> 00:14:26,824
Once I become successful,
I'll repay you all!

291
00:14:26,907 --> 00:14:27,950
-Sure.
-Bye now.

292
00:14:28,033 --> 00:14:29,618
-Bye, see you later!
-Bye!

293
00:14:29,702 --> 00:14:32,872
Wait, Pero!

294
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:35,583
Hold on, Pero!

295
00:14:35,666 --> 00:14:40,296
Pero! Wait! Pero!

296
00:14:40,379 --> 00:14:42,298
Pero!

297
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:54,393
Heave-ho!

298
00:14:55,811 --> 00:14:58,606
Heave-ho!

299
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:02,484
Oh! Heave-ho!

300
00:15:08,699 --> 00:15:09,533
Thank you.

301
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:11,201
No, thank you as well.

302
00:15:11,285 --> 00:15:13,037
-Mister, your hat is nice.
-Thank you.

303
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:15,623
-Can I have it?
-Huh? Give it back!

304
00:15:15,706 --> 00:15:18,167
Hey! Give it to me!

305
00:15:20,127 --> 00:15:22,463
Nice! Okay.

306
00:15:28,719 --> 00:15:30,012
What?

307
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:34,600
All right! One, two, three bills…

308
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:36,810
That's 15,000 yen!

309
00:15:36,894 --> 00:15:37,937
Mr. Konta!

310
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:40,147
Mr. Torihara, hello.

311
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:42,608
-Looking forward to filming today!
-No.

312
00:15:42,691 --> 00:15:46,236
-Actually, Konta, I'm heading back now.
-Huh? What?

313
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:48,864
I have already sufficiently
captured your charm.

314
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:52,451
But it has only been yesterday.
Aren't you going to film today too?

315
00:15:52,534 --> 00:15:54,912
I understand your good qualities
very well now.

316
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:57,414
-Oh, is that so?
-Yes.

317
00:15:57,498 --> 00:15:58,999
Look forward to the broadcast.

318
00:15:59,083 --> 00:15:59,917
I will.

319
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,335
Well, excuse me.

320
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:04,004
-Wait, you understand my good qualities?
-Yes!

321
00:16:04,088 --> 00:16:06,632
Okay. Wait, what are they?

322
00:16:06,715 --> 00:16:07,800
Watch it when it airs!

323
00:16:07,883 --> 00:16:10,010
No, I want to know my good qualities!

324
00:16:10,094 --> 00:16:11,762
-I can't tell you.
-I don't know…

325
00:16:11,845 --> 00:16:13,555
No? Why can't you tell me?

326
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:16,225
-Please watch it on air.
-Does that mean I don't have any?

327
00:16:16,308 --> 00:16:18,018
No, just watch the show!

328
00:16:25,317 --> 00:16:28,904
Document Memoreal<i>. I watch it too.</i>

329
00:16:29,863 --> 00:16:30,781
I see.

330
00:16:32,116 --> 00:16:34,660
You watch it too, Lady Yomi?

331
00:16:35,619 --> 00:16:40,082
<i>I like their large family special,</i>
<i>"We are! The 1,000-Person Family."</i>

332
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:45,462
<i>But it's ironic.</i>
<i>Just when he's finally getting on TV,</i>

333
00:16:45,546 --> 00:16:47,881
<i>he doesn't have long to live.</i>

334
00:16:47,965 --> 00:16:51,760
<i>Well, if he hasn't</i>
<i>become famous by that age,</i>

335
00:16:51,844 --> 00:16:54,221
<i>he isn't going to become a star now.</i>

336
00:16:54,304 --> 00:16:58,308
<i>All that's left is to quietly wait</i>
<i>for death at the end of summer.</i>

337
00:16:59,518 --> 00:17:01,520
I think so too, but…

338
00:17:08,777 --> 00:17:10,988
They pursue their dreams, have hope…

339
00:17:11,947 --> 00:17:15,367
and try to live out their days
the best they can.

340
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:18,787
That's what

341
00:17:19,788 --> 00:17:21,623
makes them human, I think.

342
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:25,085
<i>Grim Reaper.</i>

343
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:28,464
<i>You sound like a human.</i>
<i>Don't say things like that.</i>

344
00:17:30,549 --> 00:17:31,550
My apologies.

345
00:17:34,303 --> 00:17:38,307
<i>It is forbidden for a Grim Reaper</i>
<i>to feel affection for humans.</i>

346
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:41,977
<i>The fates of Grim Reapers</i>
<i>and humans do not cross.</i>

347
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:46,690
<i>You must devote yourself entirely</i>
<i>to witnessing their lifespans.</i>

348
00:17:48,275 --> 00:17:49,318
Understood.

349
00:17:51,779 --> 00:17:52,780
That is…

350
00:17:55,616 --> 00:17:57,326
my mission, after all.

351
00:18:19,306 --> 00:18:21,850
<i>-Midori, it's starting, hurry!</i>
<i>-Wait for me!</i>

352
00:18:22,476 --> 00:18:24,061
-There it is.
-It's started!

353
00:18:24,144 --> 00:18:25,020
It's started.

354
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:26,563
I am…

355
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:27,898
Konta Hoshino.

356
00:18:27,981 --> 00:18:29,274
Then please get Koji Yakusho.

357
00:18:29,358 --> 00:18:30,442
One more time!

358
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:33,320
If they edit it like that,
it will make me look bad.

359
00:18:33,403 --> 00:18:36,240
<i>The editing is just malicious, isn't it?</i>

360
00:18:36,323 --> 00:18:38,117
<i>We are unemployed, living on benefits…</i>

361
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:39,409
Jobless?

362
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:40,994
I'm being made a fool of!

363
00:18:41,078 --> 00:18:42,830
Even a tiny role. I'll do it!

364
00:18:42,913 --> 00:18:44,748
What is this? Did he secretly film me?

365
00:18:44,832 --> 00:18:47,876
<i>The heck? Mr. Torihara betrayed me.</i>

366
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:51,171
I think this episode
turned out quite well.

367
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:54,299
<i>My acting career is over.</i>

368
00:18:54,383 --> 00:18:55,342
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
